# Line endings are LF everywhere, including in the working tree.
#
# The repository already stores LF in the index for every tracked text file, and
# the token generator (scripts/generate-tokens.mjs) writes LF. With
# core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout produced CRLF working files, so after
# every `npm run tokens` or `npm run build`, git status reported
# src/styles/tokens.css as modified while git diff showed no change — a phantom
# that made it impossible to tell a clean tree from a dirty one.
#
# Setting eol=lf makes the working tree match both the index and the generator.
# This changes nothing in git's history: the stored content is already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
